# Tool working directories. None of this is project source, and the scraped pages under .firecrawl
# are not valid JSON, so prettier exits with an error rather than a warning when it reaches them.
.firecrawl
.serena
.claude
**/.claude

# Hand-maintained docs and root config.
#
# Prettier owns src/ and scripts/ and nothing else, which is exactly the set lint-staged formats on
# commit (see the lint-staged block in package.json). Anything outside that set is written by hand
# and never reformatted on the way in, so letting a manual prettier run rewrite it produces a diff
# nobody asked for and the file drifts straight back the next time someone edits it. Keeping the two
# scopes identical is what makes `prettier --check .` a no-op on a clean tree.
*.md
**/*.md
index.html
*.config.js
tsconfig*.json
.prettierrc.json
